"<div><div class=\" response-message\"></div></div><h2>Economy Forecast (6 months)</h2>\n<p>✅ Forecast complete</p>\n<p>This design follows the specific constraints: 4 resources, crafting enabled, and player-to-player trading disabled (focusing on a &quot;Trader&quot; loop with NPC stations/factions).</p>\n<hr />\n<h1>Part 1: Resource System Design</h1>\n<h3>1. Resource Identity</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr><th align=\"left\">Resource</th><th align=\"left\">Type</th><th align=\"left\">Role</th><th align=\"left\">Thematic Fit</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Galactic Credits (GC)</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Currency</td><td align=\"left\">Universal medium of exchange; used for maintenance and NPC purchases.</td><td align=\"left\">Standard space-faring currency.</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Raw Asterite</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Material</td><td align=\"left\">Foundational building block; high volume, low value per unit.</td><td align=\"left\">Mined from belts; the &quot;fuel&quot; of the industrial engine.</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Neural Chips</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Material</td><td align=\"left\">High-tier crafting component; gates advanced technology.</td><td align=\"left\">Salvaged from derelicts; represents technological complexity.</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Sector Intel</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Experience</td><td align=\"left\">Progression currency; used to unlock new star systems and tech tiers.</td><td align=\"left\">Data gathered via exploration; represents the player's &quot;level.&quot;</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>2. Generation Sources</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>GC:</strong> Earned by fulfilling NPC contracts (70%) and selling excess Asterite (30%). Scaling: +15% per Sector Tier.</li>\n<li><strong>Raw Asterite:</strong> Acquired via mining mini-games. 500–1,000 units per 10-minute session. Scaling: Better lasers increase yield.</li>\n<li><strong>Neural Chips:</strong> Rare drops from combat encounters or &quot;Deep Scan&quot; missions. 1–5 per encounter. Frequency: Low (15% drop rate).</li>\n<li><strong>Sector Intel:</strong> Passive generation during travel and active generation via scanning anomalies. Fixed rate based on &quot;Sensor Grade.&quot;</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3. Consumption Uses</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>GC:</strong> Ship repairs (Frequent/Low cost), Fuel (Frequent/Low cost), Blueprint purchases (Rare/High cost).</li>\n<li><strong>Raw Asterite:</strong> Primary ingredient for ship hulls and base components. Required in thousands.</li>\n<li><strong>Neural Chips:</strong> Required for &quot;Overclocking&quot; gear and crafting Tier 3+ modules.</li>\n<li><strong>Sector Intel:</strong> Spent on the &quot;Navigation Tree&quot; to unlock new zones and &quot;Research Tree&quot; for crafting recipes.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>4. Storage and Limits</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Storage:</strong> Ships have limited Cargo Holds for Asterite/Chips. GC and Intel are digital and unlimited.</li>\n<li><strong>Rationale:</strong> Cargo limits force players to return to hubs, creating a gameplay loop of &quot;Sortie -&gt; Harvest -&gt; Return.&quot;</li>\n<li><strong>Overflow:</strong> Excess materials are automatically converted to a small amount of GC (5% value) if the hold is full.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>5. Exchange Rates (NPC Only)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>100 Raw Asterite</strong> = 10 GC (Base Sell Price).</li>\n<li><strong>1 Neural Chip</strong> = 500 GC (High Value Salvage).</li>\n<li><strong>Intel</strong> cannot be sold; it is a non-transferable progression metric.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>6. Sink Mechanisms</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The &quot;Tax&quot; Sink:</strong> Every craft requires a GC &quot;Assembly Fee.&quot;</li>\n<li><strong>The &quot;Maintenance&quot; Sink:</strong> Ship integrity degrades over distance traveled, requiring GC for repairs.</li>\n<li><strong>The &quot;Expansion&quot; Sink:</strong> Unlocking new sectors requires exponential amounts of Intel and GC.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h1>Part 2: 6-Month Economy Forecast</h1>\n<h3>Month 1: The Gold Rush (Launch)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Player Progression:</strong> Avg. Level 10. 0% at endgame. Skill trees 15% complete.</li>\n<li><strong>Resource Abundance:</strong> Low. Players spend resources as fast as they get them. Velocity is high.</li>\n<li><strong>Economy Health:</strong> <strong>Healthy.</strong> High engagement; demand exceeds supply.</li>\n<li><strong>Adjustments:</strong> Monitor &quot;Neural Chip&quot; drop rates to ensure players don't stall at the first crafting gate.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Month 2: The Industrial Expansion</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Player Progression:</strong> Avg. Level 25. 2% (Hardcore) reaching early endgame.</li>\n<li><strong>Resource Abundance:</strong> Asterite stockpiles begin to grow in mid-tier players. GC remains stable.</li>\n<li><strong>Economy Health:</strong> <strong>Healthy.</strong> Sinks (Repairs/Fuel) are effectively removing GC.</li>\n<li><strong>Adjustments:</strong> Increase GC cost for Tier 2 Ship Blueprints to prevent &quot;Credit Bloat&quot; in Hardcore players.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Month 3: The Efficiency Gap</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Player Progression:</strong> Avg. Level 40. 10% at endgame.</li>\n<li><strong>Resource Abundance:</strong> Hardcore players have 10x the wealth of Casuals. Wealth distribution starts to skew heavily.</li>\n<li><strong>Economy Health:</strong> <strong>Stable.</strong> Minor inflation in Raw Asterite value (oversupply).</li>\n<li><strong>Adjustments:</strong> Introduce &quot;Bulk Refining&quot; – a sink that consumes massive Asterite for a small chance at rare components.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Month 4: The Tech Plateau</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Player Progression:</strong> Avg. Level 55. 25% at endgame. Skill trees 70% complete.</li>\n<li><strong>Resource Abundance:</strong> Sector Intel becomes &quot;dead weight&quot; for Hardcore players who finished the tree.</li>\n<li><strong>Economy Health:</strong> <strong>Inflated (Intel).</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Adjustments:</strong> Add &quot;Intel Sinks&quot; – allow players to spend Intel on temporary buffs (e.g., +10% Mining Yield for 1 hour).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Month 5: Saturation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Player Progression:</strong> Avg. Level 60 (Cap). 45% at endgame.</li>\n<li><strong>Resource Abundance:</strong> GC velocity slows down as players stop buying new ships and only pay for repairs.</li>\n<li><strong>Economy Health:</strong> <strong>Warning (Deflated Velocity).</strong> Players are hoarding rather than spending.</li>\n<li><strong>Adjustments:</strong> Introduce &quot;Consumable Crafting&quot; (e.g., powerful one-time-use missiles) that require Neural Chips and GC.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Month 6: Maturity &amp; Reset</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Player Progression:</strong> 65% at endgame. Hardcore players have 100% completion.</li>\n<li><strong>Resource Abundance:</strong> Massive GC reserves. Asterite is trivial.</li>\n<li><strong>Economy Health:</strong> <strong>Inflated.</strong> The economy requires a &quot;New Frontier&quot; (Expansion).</li>\n<li><strong>Adjustments:</strong> Launch &quot;Sector Tier 2&quot; – a new set of resources that requires existing resources to access, effectively resetting the value of hoarded GC.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h3>Archetype Summary (Month 6)</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr><th align=\"left\">Metric</th><th align=\"left\">Casual (1-2h/d)</th><th align=\"left\">Regular (3-4h/d)</th><th align=\"left\">Hardcore (6+h/d)</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Level</strong></td><td align=\"left\">45</td><td align=\"left\">60</td><td align=\"left\">60 (Maxed)</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>GC Holdings</strong></td><td align=\"left\">50,000</td><td align=\"left\">250,000</td><td align=\"left\">2,000,000+</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Primary Activity</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Mission Completion</td><td align=\"left\">Optimization/Crafting</td><td align=\"left\">Resource Hoarding/Min-Maxing</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Pain Point</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Neural Chip Scarcity</td><td align=\"left\">Storage Limits</td><td align=\"left\">Lack of meaningful sinks</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Final Recommended Adjustments for Long-Term Balance:</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Dynamic Pricing:</strong> Implement a &quot;Galactic Market&quot; (NPC-driven) where if players sell too much Asterite, the price drops globally for 24 hours.</li>\n<li><strong>Prestige System:</strong> Allow players to &quot;Donate&quot; maxed-out Intel to a Faction for cosmetic rewards, preventing Intel inflation.</li>\n<li><strong>Loot Table Shift:</strong> At Month 4, increase Neural Chip drops in low-level zones to help Casual players catch up to the mid-game crafting requirements.</li>\n</ol>\n<div><div class=\" completion-message response-message\"></div></div>"